rty":"R","state":"CA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-03","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Consequences for Social Security Fraud Act</strong></p><p>This bill adds additional criminal offences to the grounds upon which a non-U.S. national (<em>alien</em> under federal law) may be barred from admission into the United States or deported. Specifically, an individual who has been convicted of, or admits to committing, Social Security fraud, identification document fraud, or fraud related to COVID-19 financial assistance programs is inadmissible or deportable under the bill. <em></em></p>","updateDate":"2025-02-25T16:48:23Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Consequences for Social Security Fraud Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2025-02-25T16:48:25Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-02-25T16:48:25Z"}
